\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Provides the member typedef <code>type</code> which is the same as <code>T</code>, except that its topmost cv-qualifiers are removed.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Removes the topmost <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span></code>, or the topmost <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">volatile</span></span></code>, or both, if present.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Removes the topmost <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3)</span> Removes the topmost <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">volatile</span></span></code>.</div>\n<p>If the program adds specializations for any of the templates described on this page, the behavior is undefined.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Member_types\">Member types</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Name\n</td>\n<td> Definition\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>type</code>\n</td>\n<td> the type <code>T</code> without cv-qualifier\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Helper_types\">Helper types</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx14\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">using</span> remove_cv_t <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> remove_cv<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">type</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-si